url: https://github.com/norandom/lesscode
abstract: >-
  Lesscode is a research project on making AI-generated codebases smaller
  and less entangled while keeping their behaviour at the public surface.
  It records behaviour from the original under an effect-capturing sandbox,
  scores that recording by mutation, lets a language model regenerate one
  scope behind its derived public surface under a structural contract,
  accepts only on zero divergence, measures size and internal call edges,
  reviews independently, and searches the pure core for differences the
  recording cannot see. The repository holds the preregistered experiments,
  their receipts and the dated research log, a Kiro-style specification of
  the loop, and a native measurement core.
keywords:
  - code simplification
  - AI-generated code
  - behaviour preservation
  - differential testing
  - mutation testing
  - concolic execution
  - spec-driven development
  - research reproducibility
